While a DevTools client is attached, Ladybird sends the objects that a
page logs as grips, and keeps those of the latest 500 to 1000 messages,
dropping older ones 500 messages at a time. Gecko’s ConsoleAPIStorage
keeps the last 1000 messages of each window (STORAGE_MAX_EVENTS), and
the grips of all their arguments come from the DevTools server’s
prepareConsoleMessageForRemote(). And V8’s V8ConsoleMessageStorage keeps
at most 1000 messages and 10 MiB of them (maxConsoleMessageCount and
maxConsoleMessageV8Size), wrapping their arguments in the “console”
object group. WebKit’s InspectorConsoleAgent keeps 100 messages
(maximumConsoleMessages), and drops the oldest 10 messages at a time
(expireConsoleMessagesStep). Unlike all three, Ladybird keeps no
messages while no client is attached, since its UI process drops them.
